6185016 #edb/ref 1061 37588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185016 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a6b95b2-a3b2-5264-9183-0fefe3abfed8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185016 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186185346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185195 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186185196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185195 #edb/ref 1061 4307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185195 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83175ccc-7da0-50d9-b695-82571c0cb353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185195 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185196 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186185197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185196 #edb/ref 1061 4313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185196 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0a3a07c-d5b4-5d4b-805c-3c93987ee6fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185196 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186185310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185197 #edb/ref 1061 4314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185197 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d028b29f-988d-5038-a9c2-8a95b472232b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185197 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185310 #edb/ref 1064 "The product rule for radicals also works for higher-order roots, like the cube root. In the case of the cube root, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{ab} = \\sqrt[3]{a}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{b}.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[n]{ab} = \\sqrt[n]{a}\\cdot \\sqrt[n]{b}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185310 #edb/ref 1065 1607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185310 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f9406c08-e6de-514e-aeae-9f581d5730a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185310 #edb/ref 1067 "The Product Rule for Cube Roots" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185346 #edb/ref 1064 "The **product rule for radicals** states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\n\t}\n$$\n\nWe can use the product rule to combine radical expressions. \n\nFor example, let's suppose we want to combine the radicals in the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5x} \\cdot \\sqrt{6z}\n$$\n\nTo combine the radicals, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5x}\\cdot \\sqrt{6z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5x\\cdot 6z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{30xz} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185346 #edb/ref 1065 6200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185346 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1c9d8f0d-315b-5c83-a8e6-17638c1c3d24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185346 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502986 #edb/ref 1080 "14\\sqrt{u+v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502986 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502986 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03aa9e77-c1bd-5499-b44b-44dc50ce6ae6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502990 #edb/ref 1080 "15{z}^{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502990 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502990 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05cd87b2-a486-59e8-85ee-e76c7c31902b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502998 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt[3]{2}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502998 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502998 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "088c6b4c-b361-5d39-9983-8191161ab392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503000 #edb/ref 1080 "14\\sqrt{uv}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503000 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503000 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08f49d0c-f8bf-5cbd-b4c6-6dfe0604684e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503018 #edb/ref 1080 "{z}^{2}\\sqrt{15z}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503018 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10e1544e-48e2-5db7-a5cf-be0b233078c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503042 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt[3]{10A+B}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503042 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503042 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f45291e-26c4-5a77-a250-9b4d715